[Term]
id: GO:0001561
name: fatty acid alpha-oxidation
namespace: biological_process
def: "Pathway by which 3-methyl branched fatty acids are degraded. These compounds are not degraded by the normal peroxisomal beta-oxidation pathway, because the 3-methyl blocks the dehydrogenation of the hydroxyl group by hydroxyacyl-CoA dehydrogenase. The 3-methyl branched fatty acid is converted in several steps to pristenic acid, which can then feed into the beta-oxidative pathway." [http://www.peroxisome.org/Scientist/Biochemistry/alpha-oxidation.html]
subset: gosubset_prok
is_a: GO:0019395 ! fatty acid oxidation

