[Term]
id: GO:0002467
name: germinal center formation
namespace: biological_process
def: "The process by which germinal centers form. A germinal center is a specialized microenvironment formed when activated B cells enter lymphoid follicles. Germinal centers are the foci for B cell proliferation and somatic hypermutation." [GOC:jal, GOC:mtg_15nov05, ISBN:081533642X]
comment: This term was added by GO_REF:0000022.
