[Term]
id: GO:0002473
name: non-professional antigen presenting cell antigen processing and presentation
namespace: biological_process
def: "The process by which a non-professional antigen presenting cell expresses antigen (peptide or lipid) on its cell surface in association with an MHC protein complex. Non-professional antigen presenting cells include all cell types but dendritic cells, B cells, T cells, monocytes, macrophages, and neutrophils." [GOC:add, ISBN:0781735149 "Fundamental Immunology", PMID:15771591]
