[Term]
id: GO:0006012
name: galactose metabolic process
namespace: biological_process
def: "The chemical reactions and pathways involving galactose, the aldohexose galacto-hexose. D-galactose is widely distributed in combined form in plants, animals and microorganisms as a constituent of oligo- and polysaccharides; it also occurs in galactolipids and as its glucoside in lactose and melibiose." [ISBN:0198506732 "Oxford Dictionary of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology"]
