[Term]
id: GO:0006097
name: glyoxylate cycle
namespace: biological_process
def: "A modification of the TCA cycle occurring in some plants and microorganisms, in which isocitrate is cleaved to glyoxylate and succinate. Glyoxylate can then react with acetyl-CoA to form malate." [ISBN:0198506732 "Oxford Dictionary of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology"]
