[Term]
id: GO:0006127
name: glycerophosphate shuttle
namespace: biological_process
def: "The process of transferring reducing equivalents from the cytosol into the mitochondria; NADH is used to synthesise glycerol 3-phosphate in the cytosol; this compound is then transported into the mitochondria where it is converted to dihydroxyacetone phosphate (DHAP) using FAD; DHAP then returns to the cytosol to complete the cycle." [GOC:jl, http://cancerweb.ncl.ac.uk/]
subset: gosubset_prok
is_a: GO:0006118 ! electron transport

