[Term]
id: GO:0007580
name: extrachromosomal circular DNA accumulation during cell aging
namespace: biological_process
def: "Increase in abundance, as cells age, of circular DNA molecules that originate in the chromosome but are excised and circularized, often by intramolecular homologous recombination between direct tandem repeats, and replicated independently of chromosomal replication." [GOC:jh, PMID:9891807]
comment: Note that the term string was changed to be consistent with placement of this term in cell aging hierarchy.
