[Term]
id: GO:0007598
name: blood coagulation, extrinsic pathway
namespace: biological_process
def: "A pathway of blood coagulation in which the earlier stages of the cascade are bypassed and the activation of factor X to factor Xa is effected by the combination of factor VIIa + thromboplastin; this second pathway occurs when tissue extracts are present in optimal amounts and is much more rapid than the intrinsic pathway." [ISBN:0198506732 "Oxford Dictionary of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology"]
comment: See also the biological process term 'blood coagulation, intrinsic pathway ; GO:0007597'.
