[Term]
id: GO:0015115
name: silicate transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Enables the directed movement of silicates into, out of, within or between cells. Silicates are the salts of silicic acids, and are usually composed of silicon and oxygen (Si[x]O[y]), one or more metals, and possibly hydrogen. Types of silicate include unisilicates, metasilicates and hydrous silicates." [GOC:ai, http://cancerweb.ncl.ac.uk/]
