[Term]
id: GO:0015120
name: phosphoglycerate transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Enables the directed movement of phosphoglycerates into, out of, within or between cells. Phosphoglycerates are important intermediates in glycolysis and 3-phosphoglycerate is a precursor in serine biosynthesis." [GOC:ai]
subset: gosubset_prok
is_a: GO:0005342 ! organic acid transporter activity
is_a: GO:0008514 ! organic anion transporter activity

[Term]
id: GO:0015121
name: phosphoenolpyruvate transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Enables the directed movement of phosphoenolpyruvate into, out of, within or between cells. Phosphoenolpyruvate is the phosphate ester formed from the hydroxy group of the enol tautomer of pyruvate. It is a key intermediate in glycolysis and gluconeogenesis, and in the biosynthesis of aromatic amino acids." [GOC:ai]
is_a: GO:0008514 ! organic anion transporter activity

[Term]
id: GO:0015123
name: acetate transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Enables the directed movement of acetate into, out of, within or between cells. Acetate is the 2-carbon carboxylic acid ethanoic acid." [GOC:ai]
is_a: GO:0008028 ! monocarboxylic acid transporter activity

[Term]
id: GO:0015124
name: allantoate transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Enables the directed movement of allantoate into, out of, within or between cells. Allantoate is the end product of purine metabolism in mammals and some fish, formed form allantoin. It is widely distributed in plants as an important source of stored nitrogen." [GOC:ai, ISBN:0198547684]
is_a: GO:0008028 ! monocarboxylic acid transporter activity

[Term]
id: GO:0015125
name: bile acid transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Enables the directed movement of bile acid into, out of, within or between cells. Bile acids are any of a group of steroid carboxylic acids occurring in bile, where they are present as the sodium salts of their amides with glycine or taurine." [GOC:ai]
is_a: GO:0008028 ! monocarboxylic acid transporter activity

[Term]
id: GO:0015126
name: canalicular bile acid transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
is_a: GO:0015125 ! bile acid transporter activity

[Term]
id: GO:0015127
name: bilirubin transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Enables the directed movement of bilirubin into, out of, within or between cells. Bilirubin is a linear tetrapyrrole produced in the reticuloendothelial system from biliverdin and transported to the liver as a complex with serum albumin. In the liver, bilirubin is converted to bilirubin bisglucuronide, which is excreted in the bile." [GOC:ai, ISBN:0198547684]
is_a: GO:0008028 ! monocarboxylic acid transporter activity

[Term]
id: GO:0015128
name: gluconate transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Enables the directed movement of gluconate into, out of, within or between cells. Gluconate is the aldonic acid derived from glucose." [GOC:ai, ISBN:0198506732 "Oxford Dictionary of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology"]
subset: gosubset_prok
narrow_synonym: "L-idonate/D-gluconate:hydrogen symporter activity" []
is_a: GO:0008028 ! monocarboxylic acid transporter activity

[Term]
id: GO:0015129
name: lactate transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Enables the directed movement of lactate into, out of, within or between cells. Lactate is 2-hydroxypropanoate, CH3-CHOH-COOH; L(+)-lactate is formed by anaerobic glycolysis in animal tissues, and DL-lactate is found in sour milk, molasses and certain fruit juices." [GOC:ai, ISBN:0198506732 "Oxford Dictionary of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology"]
subset: gosubset_prok
narrow_synonym: "monocarboxylate (lactate, pyruvate, mevalonate) uptake/efflux porter activity" []
is_a: GO:0008028 ! monocarboxylic acid transporter activity

[Term]
id: GO:0015130
name: mevalonate transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Enables the directed movement of mevalonate into, out of, within or between cells. Mevalonate is the anion of mevalonic acid; its (R)-enantiomer is a strategic intermediate derived from hydroxymethylglutaryl-CoA in the biosynthesis of polyprenyl compounds." [GOC:ai, ISBN:0198506732 "Oxford Dictionary of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology"]
narrow_synonym: "monocarboxylate (lactate, pyruvate, mevalonate) uptake/efflux porter activity" []
is_a: GO:0008028 ! monocarboxylic acid transporter activity

[Term]
id: GO:0015131
name: oxaloacetate transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Enables the directed movement of oxaloacetate, the anion of oxobutanedioic acid, into, out of, within or between cells." [GOC:ai]
is_a: GO:0005310 ! dicarboxylic acid transporter activity

[Term]
id: GO:0015132
name: prostaglandin transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Enables the directed movement of prostaglandins into, out of, within or between cells. A prostaglandin is any of a group of biologically active metabolites which contain a cyclopentane ring due to the formation of a bond between two carbons of a fatty acid. They have a wide range of biological activities." [GOC:ai]
broad_synonym: "prostaglandin/thromboxane transporter activity" []
is_a: GO:0008028 ! monocarboxylic acid transporter activity

[Term]
id: GO:0015133
name: uronic acid transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Enables the directed movement of uronic acid into, out of, within or between cells. Uronic acids are any monocarboxylic acid formally derived by oxidizing to a carboxyl group the terminal hydroxymethylene group of either an aldose with four or more carbon atoms in the molecule, or of any glycoside derived from such an aldose." [GOC:ai]
subset: gosubset_prok
is_a: GO:0008028 ! monocarboxylic acid transporter activity

[Term]
id: GO:0015134
name: hexuronate transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Enables the directed movement of hexuronates into, out of, within or between cells. A hexuronate is any monocarboxylic acid derived from a hexose by oxidation of C-6." [GOC:ai, ISBN:0198506732 "Oxford Dictionary of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology"]
subset: gosubset_prok
is_a: GO:0015133 ! uronic acid transporter activity

[Term]
id: GO:0015135
name: glucuronate transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Enables the directed movement of glucuronate into, out of, within or between cells. Glucuronate is the uronic acid formally derived from glucose by oxidation of the hydroxymethylene group at C-6 to a carboxyl group." [GOC:ai]
is_a: GO:0015134 ! hexuronate transporter activity

[Term]
id: GO:0015136
name: sialic acid transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Enables the directed movement of sialic acid into, out of, within or between cells." [GOC:jl]
subset: gosubset_prok
is_a: GO:0008028 ! monocarboxylic acid transporter activity
is_a: GO:0015144 ! carbohydrate transporter activity

[Term]
id: GO:0015137
name: citrate transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Enables the directed movement of citrate, 2-hydroxy-1,2,3-propanetricarboyxlate, into, out of, within or between cells." [GOC:ai]
subset: gosubset_prok
is_a: GO:0015142 ! tricarboxylic acid transporter activity

[Term]
id: GO:0015138
name: fumarate transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Enables the directed movement of fumarate into, out of, within or between cells. Fumarate is a key intermediate in metabolism and is formed in the TCA cycle from succinate and converted into malate." [GOC:ai]
narrow_synonym: "dicarboxylate (succinate/fumarate/malate) antiporter activity" []
is_a: GO:0005310 ! dicarboxylic acid transporter activity

[Term]
id: GO:0015139
name: alpha-ketoglutarate transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Enables the directed movement of alpha-ketoglutarate into, out of, within or between cells. Alpha-ketoglutarate (or oxoglutarate) is a compound with important roles in carbohydrate and amino acid metabolism, especially in transamination reactions and as a component of the TCA cycle." [GOC:ai, ISBN:0198547684]
subset: gosubset_prok
exact_synonym: "2-oxoglutarate transporter" []
is_a: GO:0005310 ! dicarboxylic acid transporter activity

[Term]
id: GO:0015140
name: malate transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Enables the directed movement of malate into, out of, within or between cells. Malate is a chiral hydroxydicarboxylic acid, hydroxybutanedioic acid. The (+) enantiomer is an important intermediate in metabolism as a component of both the TCA cycle and the glyoxylate cycle." [GOC:ai]
narrow_synonym: "dicarboxylate (succinate/fumarate/malate) antiporter activity" []
is_a: GO:0005310 ! dicarboxylic acid transporter activity

[Term]
id: GO:0015141
name: succinate transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Enables the directed movement of succinate, the dianion of ethane dicarboxylic acid, into, out of, within or between cells." [ISBN:0198506732 "Oxford Dictionary of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology"]
subset: gosubset_prok
narrow_synonym: "dicarboxylate (succinate/fumarate/malate) antiporter activity" []
is_a: GO:0005310 ! dicarboxylic acid transporter activity

