name: urate transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Enables the directed movement of urate into, out of, within or between cells. Urate is the anion of uric acid, 2,6,8-trioxypurine, the end product of purine metabolism in certain mammals and the main excretory product in uricotelic animals." [GOC:ai]
xref_analog: TC:9.B.9.1.1
is_a: GO:0005342 ! organic acid transporter activity

[Term]
id: GO:0015144
name: carbohydrate transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Enables the directed movement of carbohydrate into, out of, within or between cells." [GOC:jl]
subset: gosubset_prok
narrow_synonym: "sugar transporter" []
is_a: GO:0005215 ! transporter activity

[Term]
id: GO:0015145
name: monosaccharide transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Enables the directed movement of monosaccharide into, out of, within or between cells." [GOC:jl]
subset: gosubset_prok
is_a: GO:0051119 ! sugar transporter activity

[Term]
id: GO:0015146
name: pentose transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Enables the directed movement of a pentose sugar, a monosaccharide with 5 carbon atoms, into, out of, within or between cells." [GOC:ai]
subset: gosubset_prok
is_a: GO:0015145 ! monosaccharide transporter activity

[Term]
id: GO:0015147
name: L-arabinose transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Enables the directed movement of L-arabinose into, out of, within or between cells. Arabinose occurs free, for example in the heartwood of many conifers and in the combined states, in both furanose and pyranose forms, as a constituent of various plant hemicelluloses, bacterial polysaccharides, etc." [ISBN:0198506732 "Oxford Dictionary of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology"]
subset: gosubset_prok
narrow_synonym: "L-arabinose/beta-D-thiogalactopyranoside:hydrogen antiporter activity" []
is_a: GO:0042900 ! arabinose transporter activity

[Term]
id: GO:0015148
name: D-xylose transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Enables the directed movement of D-xylose into, out of, within or between cells. D-xylose (the naturally occurring enantiomer is always D-) is a constituent of plant polysaccharides." [ISBN:0198506732 "Oxford Dictionary of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology"]
subset: gosubset_prok
is_a: GO:0015146 ! pentose transporter activity

[Term]
id: GO:0015149
name: hexose transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Enables the directed movement of a hexose sugar, a monosaccharide with 6 carbon atoms, into, out of, within or between cells." [GOC:ai]
subset: gosubset_prok
is_a: GO:0015145 ! monosaccharide transporter activity

[Term]
id: GO:0015150
name: fucose transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Enables the directed movement of fucose into, out of, within or between cells. Fucose is 6-deoxygalactose and has two enantiomers, D-fucose and L-fucose." [GOC:ai]
subset: gosubset_prok
is_a: GO:0015149 ! hexose transporter activity

[Term]
id: GO:0015151
name: alpha-glucoside transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Enables the directed movement of alpha-glucosides into, out of, within or between cells. Alpha-glucosides are glycosides in which the sugar moiety is a glucose residue, and the anomeric carbon of the bond is in an alpha configuration." [GOC:jl, http://www.biochem.purdue.edu/, ISBN:0198506732 "Oxford Dictionary of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology"]
is_a: GO:0042947 ! glucoside transporter activity

[Term]
id: GO:0015152
name: glucose-6-phosphate transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Enables the directed movement of glucose-6-phosphate into, out of, within or between cells. Glucose-6-phosphate is a monophosphorylated derivative of glucose with the phosphate group attached to C-6." [GOC:ai]
is_a: GO:0015119 ! hexose phosphate transporter activity

[Term]
id: GO:0015153
name: rhamnose transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Enables the directed movement of rhamnose into, out of, within or between cells. Rhamnose occurs commonly as a compound of plant glycosides, in polysaccharides of gums and mucilages, and in bacterial polysaccharides. It is also a component of some plant cell wall polysaccharides and frequently acts as the sugar components of flavonoids." [GOC:ai]
subset: gosubset_prok
is_a: GO:0015149 ! hexose transporter activity

[Term]
id: GO:0015154
name: disaccharide transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Enables the directed movement of disaccharide into, out of, within or between cells." [GOC:jl]
subset: gosubset_prok
is_a: GO:0051119 ! sugar transporter activity

[Term]
id: GO:0015155
name: lactose transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Enables the directed movement of lactose into, out of, within or between cells. Lactose is a disaccharide 4-O-beta-D-galactopyranosyl-D-glucose, and constitutes roughly 5% of the milk in almost all mammals." [ISBN:0198506732 "Oxford Dictionary of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology"]
subset: gosubset_prok
narrow_synonym: "lactose/glucose efflux transporter activity" []
is_a: GO:0015154 ! disaccharide transporter activity

[Term]
id: GO:0015156
name: melibiose transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Enables the directed movement of melibiose into, out of, within or between cells. Melibiose is the disaccharide 6-O-alpha-D-galactopyranosyl-D-glucose and occurs as a constituent of the trisaccharide raffinose or in the exudates and nectaries of a number of plants." [ISBN:0198506732 "Oxford Dictionary of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology"]
subset: gosubset_prok
is_a: GO:0015154 ! disaccharide transporter activity

[Term]
id: GO:0015157
name: oligosaccharide transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Enables the directed movement of oligosaccharide into, out of, within or between cells." [GOC:jl]
subset: gosubset_prok
narrow_synonym: "endosomal oligosaccharide transporter" []
is_a: GO:0015144 ! carbohydrate transporter activity

[Term]
id: GO:0015158
name: raffinose transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Enables the directed movement of raffinose into, out of, within or between cells. Raffinose occurs in plants almost as commonly as sucrose and is present in cereal grains, cotton seeds, and many legumes. It is synthesized from sucrose by transfer of a galactopyranoside from myo-inositol." [ISBN:0198506732 "Oxford Dictionary of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology"]
is_a: GO:0015157 ! oligosaccharide transporter activity

[Term]
id: GO:0015159
name: polysaccharide transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Enables the directed movement of polysaccharides into, out of, within or between cells. A polysaccharide is a polymer of more than about 10 monosaccharide residues joined by glycosidic linkages." [GOC:ai]
subset: gosubset_prok
is_a: GO:0015144 ! carbohydrate transporter activity

[Term]
id: GO:0015160
name: beta-glucan transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Enables the directed movement of beta-glucans into, out of, within or between cells. Beta-glucans are compounds composed of glucose residues linked by beta-glucosidic bonds." [GOC:ai]
is_a: GO:0015159 ! polysaccharide transporter activity

[Term]
id: GO:0015161
name: capsular-polysaccharide transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Enables the directed movement of capsular-polysaccharides into, out of, within or between cells. Capsular polysaccharides make up the capsule, a protective structure surrounding some species of bacteria and fungi." [GOC:ai]
subset: gosubset_prok
exact_synonym: "capsule polysaccharide transporter activity" []
is_a: GO:0015159 ! polysaccharide transporter activity

[Term]
id: GO:0015162
name: teichoic acid transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Enables the directed movement of teichoic acid into, out of, within or between cells. Teichoic acid is any polymer occurring in the cell wall, membrane or capsule of Gram-positive bacteria and containing chains of glycerol phosphate or ribitol phosphate residues." [GOC:ai]
subset: gosubset_prok
is_a: GO:0015159 ! polysaccharide transporter activity

[Term]
id: GO:0015163
name: hexuronide transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Enables the directed movement of hexuronide into, out of, within or between cells. Hexuronides are any compound formed by combination of glycosidic linkage of a hydroxy compound (e.g. an alcohol or a saccharide) with the anomeric carbon atom of a hexuronate." [GOC:ai]
subset: gosubset_prok
is_a: GO:0015144 ! carbohydrate transporter activity

[Term]
id: GO:0015164
name: glucuronoside transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Enables the directed movement of glucuronosides into, out of, within or between cells. Glucuronosides are any compound formed by combination of glycosidic linkage of a hydroxy compound (e.g. an alcohol or a saccharide) with the anomeric carbon atom of glucuronate." [GOC:ai]
subset: gosubset_prok
exact_synonym: "glucuronide transporter activity" []
is_a: GO:0015163 ! hexuronide transporter activity

[Term]
id: GO:0015165
name: pyrimidine nucleotide sugar transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Enables the directed movement of pyrimidine nucleotide-sugars into, out of, within or between cells. Pyrimidine nucleotide-sugars are pyrimidine nucleotides in glycosidic linkage with a monosaccharide or monosaccharide derivative." [GOC:ai]
is_a: GO:0005338 ! nucleotide-sugar transporter activity

[Term]
id: GO:0015166
name: polyol transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Enables the directed movement of polyols, polyhydric alcohols, into, out of, within or between cells." [ISBN:0198506732 "Oxford Dictionary of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology"]
subset: gosubset_prok
narrow_synonym: "sugar/polyol channel activity" []
is_a: GO:0015665 ! alcohol transporter activity

[Term]
id: GO:0015167
name: arabitol transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Enables the directed movement of arabitol into, out of, within or between cells. Arabitol is the pentitol derived from arabinose or lyxose by reduction of the aldehyde group. The D enantiomer is present in lichens and mushrooms." [ISBN:0198506732 "Oxford Dictionary of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology"]
exact_synonym: "arabinitol transporter activity" []
is_a: GO:0015166 ! polyol transporter activity

[Term]
id: GO:0015168
name: glycerol transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Enables the directed movement of glycerol into, out of, within or between cells. Glycerol is 1,2,3-propanetriol, a sweet, hygroscopic, viscous liquid, widely distributed in nature as a constituent of many lipids." [GOC:ai]
subset: gosubset_prok
is_a: GO:0015166 ! polyol transporter activity

[Term]
id: GO:0015169
name: glycerol-3-phosphate transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Enables the directed movement of glycerol-3-phosphate into, out of, within or between cells. Glycerol-3-phosphate is a phosphoric monoester of glycerol." [GOC:ai]
subset: gosubset_prok
is_a: GO:0015168 ! glycerol transporter activity

[Term]
id: GO:0015170
name: propanediol transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Enables the directed movement of propanediol into, out of, within or between cells. Propanediol is a sweet colorless, viscous, hygroscopic liquid used as an antifreeze and in brake fluid; it is also as a humectant in cosmetics and personal care items, although it can be absorbed through the skin with harmful effects." [GOC:ai]
is_a: GO:0015166 ! polyol transporter activity

[Term]
id: GO:0015171
name: amino acid transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Enables the directed movement of amino acids, organic acids containing one or more amino substituents, into, out of, within or between cells." [GOC:ai]
subset: gosubset_prok
narrow_synonym: "amino acid/choline transporter activity" []
is_a: GO:0005275 ! amine transporter activity
is_a: GO:0046943 ! carboxylic acid transporter activity

[Term]
id: GO:0015172
