is_a: GO:0015171 ! amino acid transporter activity

[Term]
id: GO:0015174
name: basic amino acid transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Enables the directed movement of basic amino acids, amino acids with a pH above 7, into, out of, within or between cells." [GOC:ai]
subset: gosubset_prok
is_a: GO:0015171 ! amino acid transporter activity

[Term]
id: GO:0015175
name: neutral amino acid transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Enables the directed movement of neutral amino acids, amino acids with no net charge, into, out of, within or between cells." [GOC:ai]
subset: gosubset_prok
is_a: GO:0015171 ! amino acid transporter activity

[Term]
id: GO:0015176
name: holin
namespace: molecular_function
def: "OBSOLETE. Primary function of holins appears to be transport of murein hydrolases across the cytoplasmic membrane to the cell wall of bacteria, where these enzymes hydrolyze the cell wall polymer as a prelude to cell lysis. When chromosomally encoded, these enzymes are therefore autolysins. Holins may also facilitate leakage of electrolytes and nutrients from the cell cytoplasm, thereby promoting cell death. Some catalyze export of nucleases." [TC:1.A.38.-.-]
comment: This term was made obsolete because it represents a class of gene products. To update annotations, consider biological_process term 'cytolysis ; GO:0019835' or its children and molecular_function term 'protein transporter activity ; GO:0008565' or its children.
is_obsolete: true

