def: "Enables the directed movement of urea into, out of, within or between cells. Urea is the water soluble compound H2N-CO-NH2, produced in the liver via the ornithine-urea cycle. It is the main nitrogen-containing (urinary) excretion product in ureotelic animals." [ISBN:0198506732 "Oxford Dictionary of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology"]
