[Term]
id: GO:0015708
name: silicate transport
namespace: biological_process
def: "The directed movement of silicates into, out of, within or between cells. Silicates are the salts of silicic acids, and are usually composed of silicon and oxygen (Si[x]O[y]), one or more metals, and possibly hydrogen. Types of silicate include unisilicates, metasilicates and hydrous silicates." [GOC:krc]
