[Term]
id: GO:0016006
name: Nebenkern
namespace: cellular_component
def: "A product of the fusion of the mitochondria during spermatogenesis. After the completion of meiosis the mitochondria of the spermatid collect along side the nucleus and fuse into two masses; these wrap around each other to produce the spherical Nebenkern. During flagellum elongation the Nebenkern unfolds and the two derivatives (major and minor mitochondrial derivatives) elongate down the axoneme." [GOC:ma]
is_a: GO:0005739 ! mitochondrion

[Term]
id: GO:0016007
name: mitochondrial derivative
namespace: cellular_component
def: "The major and minor mitochondrial derivatives are the mitochondria of the sperm tail and derive by the unfolding of the Nebenkern during flagellum elongation." [GOC:ma]
