[Term]
id: GO:0016068
name: type I hypersensitivity
namespace: biological_process
def: "An inflammatory response driven by antigen recognition by antibodies bound to Fc receptors on mast cells or basophils, occurring within minutes after exposure of a sensitized individual to the antigen, and leading to the release of a variety of inflammatory mediators such as histamines." [GOC:add, ISBN:0781735149 "Fundamental Immunology"]
comment: Note that localized and systemic anaphylaxis is usually a result of type I hypersensitivity.
exact_synonym: "immediate hypersensitivity response" []
