[Term]
id: GO:0019049
name: evasion of host defenses by virus
namespace: biological_process
def: "Any process, either active or passive, by which a virus avoids or tolerates the effects of its host organism's defense(s). Host defenses may be induced by the presence of the virus or may be preformed (e.g. physical barriers). The host is defined as the larger of the organisms involved in a symbiotic interaction." [ISBN:1555811272]
