[Term]
id: GO:0021614
name: glossopharyngeal nerve maturation
namespace: biological_process
def: "A developmental process, independent of morphogenetic (shape) change, that is required for the glossopharyngeal nerve to attain its fully functional state. Various sensory and motor branches of the glossopharyngeal nerve supply nerve connections to the pharynx and back of the tongue. The branchial motor component contains motor fibers that innervate muscles that elevate the pharynx and larynx, and the tympanic branch supplies parasympathetic fibers to the otic ganglion." [GOC:cls, GOC:dgh, GOC:dph, GOC:jic, GOC:mtg_15jun06, ISBN:0838580343]
comment: This term was added by GO_REF:0000021.
related_synonym: "CN IX maturation" []
is_a: GO:0021605 ! cranial nerve maturation
relationship: part_of GO:0021563 ! glossopharyngeal nerve development

