[Term]
id: GO:0021618
name: hypoglossal nerve morphogenesis
namespace: biological_process
def: "The process by which the anatomical structure of the hypoglossal nerve is generated and organized. Morphogenesis pertains to the creation of form. This motor nerve innervates all the intrinsic and all but one of the extrinsic muscles of the tongue." [GOC:cls, GOC:dgh, GOC:dph, GOC:jic, GOC:mtg_15jun06, ISBN:0838580343]
