[Term]
id: GO:0021651
name: rhombomere 1 morphogenesis
namespace: biological_process
def: "The process by which the anatomical structure of rhombomere 1 is generated and organized. Morphogenesis pertains to the creation of form. Rhombomeres are transverse segments of the developing rhombencephalon. Rhombomeres are lineage restricted, express different genes from one another, and adopt different developmental fates. Rhombomeres are numbered in an anterior to posterior order." [GOC:cls, GOC:curators, GOC:dgh, GOC:dph, GOC:jic, GOC:mtg_15jun06]
comment: This term was added by GO_REF:0000021.
