[Term]
id: GO:0022002
name: wnt receptor signaling involved in negative regulation of anterior neural cell fate of the neural plate
namespace: biological_process
def: "The series of molecular signals that stops, prevents or reduces the frequency, rate or extent of the directed movement of a cell from adopting an anterior neural cell fate, initiated by binding of Wnt protein to a receptor on the surface of the target cell." [GOC:cls, GOC:dgh, GOC:dph, GOC:jic, GOC:mtg_15jun06]
