[Term]
id: GO:0031173
name: otolith mineralization (sensu Tetrapoda)
namespace: biological_process
def: "The formation of otoconia by precipitation of specific crystal forms of calcium carbonate around an organic core of extracellular matrix proteins. Otoconia are small (~10 micron) dense extracellular particles present in the otolith end organs of the vertebrate inner ear. As in, but not restricted to, the tetrapods (Tetrapoda, ncbi_taxonomy_id:32523)." [GOC:dsf, PMID:15581873]
exact_synonym: "otoconia mineralization" []
exact_synonym: "otoconium mineralization" []
