[Term]
id: GO:0031960
name: response to corticosteroid stimulus
namespace: biological_process
def: "A change in state or activity of a cell or an organism (in terms of movement, secretion, enzyme production, gene expression, etc.) as a result of a corticosteroid hormone stimulus. A corticosteroid is a steroid hormone that is produced in the adrenal cortex. Corticosteroids are involved in a wide range of physiologic systems such as stress response, immune response and regulation of inflammation, carbohydrate metabolism, protein catabolism, blood electrolyte levels, and behavior. They include glucocorticoids and mineralocorticoids." [GOC:mah, PMID:11027914]
is_a: GO:0048545 ! response to steroid hormone stimulus

