[Term]
id: GO:0042499
name: signal peptide peptidase activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Catalysis of the intramembrane proteolysis of a signal peptide, following its removal from a preprotein." [PMID:12077416]
comment: Note that this function is distinct from the 'signal peptidases' (see the molecular function term 'signal peptidase activity ; GO:0009003' and its children). Broadly, signal peptidases cleave N-terminal leader sequences from secreted or membrane proteins, thereby creating signal peptides, while signal peptide peptidases cleave the signal peptides themselves.
exact_synonym: "SPP" []
xref_analog: EC:3.4.23.-
is_a: GO:0042500 ! aspartic endopeptidase activity, intramembrane cleaving

[Term]
id: GO:0042500
name: aspartic endopeptidase activity, intramembrane cleaving
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Catalysis of the hydrolysis of nonterminal peptide linkages in oligopeptides or polypeptides, occurring within the plasma membrane." [GOC:jl, ISBN:0198506732 "Oxford Dictionary of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology"]
comment: Note that although GO generally avoids the use of localization information in terms, in this case an exception was made. This is because the fact that the cleavage occurs within the membrane is integral to its function, as it is the only thing that distinguishes this group from other aspartic endopeptidases.
xref_analog: EC:3.4.23.-
is_a: GO:0004190 ! aspartic-type endopeptidase activity

