[Term]
id: GO:0044413
name: avoidance of host defenses
namespace: biological_process
def: "Any process, either constitutive or induced, by which an organism evades, suppresses or tolerates the effects of its host organism's defense(s). Host defenses may be induced by the presence of the organism or may be preformed (e.g. physical barriers). The host is defined as the larger of the organisms involved in a symbiotic interaction." [GOC:mtg_pamgo_17jul06]
subset: gosubset_prok
exact_synonym: "avoidance of host defenses" []
is_a: GO:0051701 ! interaction with host
