is_a: GO:0052200 ! response to host defenses

[Term]
id: GO:0044414
name: suppression of host defenses
namespace: biological_process
def: "Any process by which an organism stops, prevents or reduces the frequency, rate or extent of host defense(s) by active mechanisms that normally result in the shutting down of a host pathway. The host is defined as the larger of the organisms involved in a symbiotic interaction." [GOC:cc]
subset: gosubset_prok
exact_synonym: "negative regulation of host defenses" []
