[Term]
id: GO:0048673
name: collateral sprouting of intact axon in response to injury
namespace: biological_process
def: "The process by which outgrowths develop from the axons of intact undamaged neurons as a result of injury to an axon. The collateral sprouts typically appear from undamaged axons in a tissue which has had part of its nerve supply removed, and they can often innervate successfully any cells that have lost some or all of their original synaptic input." [GOC:dgh, GOC:dph, GOC:jic]
