[Term]
id: GO:0050733
name: RS domain binding
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Interacting selectively with an RS domain of a protein; RS domains are usually highly phosphorylated and characterized by the presence of arginine (R)/serine (S) dipeptides. The RS domain promotes protein-protein interactions and directs subcellular localization and, in certain situations, nucleocytoplasmic shuttling of individual SR proteins. They also play a role in splicing." [PMID:11684676, PMID:12215544]
