def: "OBSOLETE. Any process by which an organism modulates the frequency, rate or extent of systemic acquired resistance in the symbiont organism; systemic acquired resistance is a salicylic acid-mediated response that confers broad spectrum systemic resistance. The symbiont is defined as the smaller of the organisms involved in a symbiotic interaction." [PAMGO:mtg]
comment: This term was made obsolete because it does not represent a real biological process.
is_obsolete: true

