namespace: biological_process
def: "The process whereby a relatively unspecialized cell acquires specialized features of a cardiac muscle cell in the atrium. Cardiac muscle cells are striated muscle cells that are responsible for heart contraction. The atrium is the part of the heart that allows blood to return to the organ." [GOC:devbiol]
exact_synonym: "atrial heart muscle cell differentiation" []
is_a: GO:0055007 ! cardiac muscle cell differentiation

[Term]
id: GO:0055012
